    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="46f56534-67cf-5d02-b0e2-edd8185f88b9" activityNameId="2d5f3336-b19c-568b-bfde-0a86826cad98" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hazardous waste incineration plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hazardous waste incineration plant
adapted from municipal waste incineration plant with a factor of 0.36. 20000 tons of waste per year. Operation time 40 years.;
Synonyms: HWI, SAVA; 
UUID: 9ee33d34-8aa5-373b-9848-9f7253a264eb
plant building infrastructure and demolition, land occupations and transformations
Location: Based on technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Well applicable to modern incineration practices in Europe or North America or Japan.
Technology: Swiss HWI plant in 2000 with wet flue gas scrubber and low-dust SCR DeNOx facility. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 2 Swiss HWI plants with a total capacity of 53'000 t/a.
Sampling: The 2 Swiss HWI plants, used as the inventory reference technology mix, have a total annual capacity of 53'000 tons of hazardous waste. This corresonds to 39% of the Swiss total installed capacity in 2000. Swiss average plants size is 20'000 t/a. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9ee33d34-8aa5-373b-9848-9f7253a264eb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
